From 0a48f5c9d53203e130e2858e6527912f578667b0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <assistant@local>
Date: Mon, 27 Jul 2026 11:17:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat: paste-to-PDF book generator with templates, reusable
 blocks, and YouTube cards

New /admin/books/from-text page: paste markdown, pick a template,
click Generate -- reuses the existing StudyNoteDocument rendering
pipeline (react-pdf + Supabase storage upload + books table insert)
instead of building a new one.

- lib/pdf/themes.js: 6 templates (Brand, Modern, Workbook, Premium,
  Minimal, Dark) as color overrides on top of the existing brand.js
  info. Header/Footer/BrandLayout/CoverPage all take an optional
  'theme' prop defaulting to 'brand', so StudyNoteDocument (unchanged)
  renders exactly as before.
- lib/pdf/calloutTypes.js + parseMarkdown.js: adds ":::type ... :::"
  fenced blocks (summary, tip, warning, memory, challenge, exercise,
  takeaway, further) and ":::checklist" as new parseable block types,
  alongside the existing headings/lists/tables/images.
- lib/pdf/youtube.js: detects bare YouTube URLs and enriches them via
  YouTube's public oEmbed endpoint (title/channel/thumbnail, no API key)
  into video cards. Runs before rendering since react-pdf builds its
  tree synchronously.
- lib/pdf/BookDocument.js: generalized sibling of StudyNoteDocument that
  takes pre-parsed+enriched blocks instead of raw markdown, plus a
  themeKey, and renders the 3 new block types.
- app/api/admin/books/from-text/route.js: parse -> enrich -> render ->
  upload to the 'books' storage bucket -> insert/update books row.
- supabase/migrations/20260727_book_source_columns.sql: adds nullable
  source_markdown + template columns to books so generated books can be
  reopened and regenerated later.
